{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "MAT",
  "chapter": 15,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then came to Jesus scribes and Pharisees, who were of Jerusalem, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why do thy disciples transgress the tradition of the elders? for they wash not their hands when they eat bread.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he answered and said to them, Why do ye also transgress the commandment of God by your tradition?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For God commanded, saying, Honor thy father and mother: and, He that curseth father or mother, let him die the death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But ye say, Whoever shall say to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " father or ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mother, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a gift, by whatever thou mightest be profited by me;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And honor not his father or his mother, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he shall be free",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Thus have ye made the commandment of God of no effect by your tradition.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hypocrites, well did Isaiah prophesy of you, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This people draw nigh to me with their mouth, and honor me with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " lips; but their heart is far from me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But in vain they do worship me, teaching ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " doctrines the commandments of men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he called the multitude, and said to them, Hear, and understand:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Not that which goeth into the mouth defileth a man; but that which cometh out of the mouth, this defileth a man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then came his disciples, and said to him, Knowest thou that the Pharisees were offended after they heard this saying?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he answered and said, Every plant, which my heavenly Father hath not planted, shall be extirpated.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them alone: they are blind leaders of the blind. And if the blind leadeth the blind, both will fall into the ditch.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then answered Peter and said to him, Declare to us this parable.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jesus said, Are ye also yet without understanding?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do ye not yet understand, that whatever entereth in at the mouth goeth into the belly, and is cast out into the draught?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But those things which proceed out of the mouth come forth from the heart; and they defile the man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For out of the heart proceed evil thoughts, murders, adulteries, fornications, thefts, false witness, blasphemies:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These are ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " which defile a man: but to eat with unwashen hands defileth not a man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Jesus went thence, and departed into the territories of Tyre and Sidon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And behold, a woman of Canaan came out of the same territories, and cried to him, saying, Have mercy on me, O Lord, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thou",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " son of David; my daughter is grievously afflicted with a demon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he answered her not a word. And his disciples came and besought him, saying, Send her away; for she crieth after us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he answered and said, I am not sent but to the lost sheep of the house of Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then came she and worshiped him, saying, Lord, help me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he answered and said, It is not meet to take the children's bread, and to cast ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to dogs.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And she said, Truth, Lord: yet the dogs eat of the crums which fall from their master's table.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Jesus answered and said to her, O woman, great ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy faith: be it to thee even as thou wilt. And her daughter was healed from that very hour.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jesus departed from thence, and came nigh to the sea of Galilee; and ascended a mountain, and sat down there.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And great multitudes came to him, having with them ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "those that were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " lame, blind, dumb, maimed, and many others, and cast them down at Jesus' feet; and he healed them:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So that the multitude wondered, when they saw the dumb to speak, the maimed to be whole, the lame to walk, and the blind to see: and they glorified the God of Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Jesus called his disciples ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and said, I have compassion on the multitude, because they continue with me now three days, and have nothing to eat: and I will not send them away fasting, lest they faint in the way.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And his disciples say to him, Whence should we have so much bread in the wilderness, as to satisfy so great a multitude?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jesus saith to them, How many loaves have ye? And they said, Seven, and a few little fishes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he commanded the multitude to sit on the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he took the seven loaves and the fishes, and gave thanks, and broke ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and gave to his disciples, and the disciples to the multitude.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they all ate and were filled: and they took up of the fragments that were left seven baskets full.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they that had eaten were four thousand men, besides women and children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.15.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.15.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he sent away the multitude, and took a boat, and came into the borders of Magdala.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
